 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent at a press conference today in Washington, D.C. Photo: Kent Nishimura/AFP via Getty Images 🇮🇷 Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent announced Operation Economic Outcast: The U.S. will impose punishing sanctions on countries and entities that do business with Iran — an attempt to bring the country to heel absent renewed military strikes. More from Barak Ravid . 📰 An independent arbitrator ruled that former Washington Post columnist Karen Attiah was wrongfully terminated last year over social posts tied to the death of Charlie Kirk, and ordered her reinstated with back pay and lost benefits. More from Sara Fischer . 🇨🇦 President Trump threatened to hit imported cars, trucks, automobile parts and steel from Canada with 50% tariffs starting on Jan. 1. He wrote on Truth Social : "Canada has been ripping off the United States of America for years. Their ridiculously high tariffs on our Farmers and farm products has made life impossible for these great American Patriots, and has long created a 60 Billion Dollar Deficit between our two Countries." Go deeper . 🏈 San Francisco 49ers owner Jed York was arrested over the weekend in Ohio and pleaded no contest to misdemeanor charges of disorderly conduct and possessing criminal tools. Go deeper . 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 4. 🐦 1 fun thing: Texting for the birds 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Natalie Peeples/Axios A pair of new apps let users send messages at the speed of a carrier pigeon — or a snail or penguin, The New York Times reports. 

 Carrier Pidge and Roost are meant to evoke the slower, riskier messaging styles of yesteryear. 🪦 Plot twist: On Carrier Pidge, the digital pigeons sometimes get lost or die en route, just like their physical counterparts.

 User Olivia Macdonald tells The Times: "The uncertainty of that, compared to the numbness that we feel receiving so many texts and notifications a day, is something that I just find really attractive about it." Gift link . 

 
 
